{"id": "EUVD-2026-81141", "enisaUuid": "785912dc-9306-365e-af6a-44f24f2cd14e", "description": "A vulnerability in a specific file download API of Cisco Secure FMC Software could allow an authenticated, remote attacker to download arbitrary files from an affected system.\r\n\r\nThis vulnerability exists because user input is not being sanitized. An attacker could exploit this vulnerability by sending a crafted HTTPS request. A successful exploit could allow the attacker to download arbitrary files from the affected system.\r\nTo exploit this vulnerability, the attacker must have valid credentials for a user account with at least the role of Security Analyst (read-only).", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T20:15:43", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-17T13:40:58", "baseScore": 7.7, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:N/A:N", "references": ["https://sec.cloudapps.cisco.com/security/center/content/CiscoSecurityAdvisory/cisco-sa-fmc-mulivulns-4PsnFwvx"], "aliases": ["GHSA-2784-9wmv-5cq2", "CVE-2026-20342"], "assigner": "cisco", "epss": 0.55, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "036ce904-a9d7-3374-bfc0-fe1f0abc524d", "product": {"name": "Cisco Secure Firewall Management Center (FMC)", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "7.0.4"}, {"id": "078eb1f9-b91a-3d91-a57c-6b62d7fb96c5", "product": {"name": "Cisco Secure Firewall Management Center (FMC)", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "7.0.9"}, {"id": "09ab707c-e3d5-35c8-a344-7c3614d9a97c", "product": {"name": "Cisco Secure Firewall Management Center (FMC)", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "7.2.1"}, {"id": "14473644-1e9e-39a3-840d-6e24ff4f1d1b", "product": {"name": "Cisco Secure Firewall Management Center (FMC)", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "7.0.2.1"}, {"id": "15344f90-e034-3ba7-b3e8-192ff363b56b", "product": {"name": "Cisco Secure Firewall Management Center (FMC)", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "7.0.6"}, {"id": "1ad7d78f